        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: стыд",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "стыд (styd) — \"shame\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "От стыда он не мог сказать ни слова. Ot stydá on ne mog skazát ni slóva. He couldn't say a word for shame."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine; genitive стыда. Мне стыдно — I feel ashamed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "стыд (styd) is inherited from Proto-Slavic stydъ (EtymDB); it is usually linked to the root of стыть 'to grow cold'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
